# Summary

=== layout: bookend

# Key Takeaways

@body

- State the claim and the evidence that supports it.
- Separate a lab result, a result in animals, and a benefit to people.
- Ask whose consent is needed and who will bear the risk.
- Compare alternatives before deciding what you would allow.

@citation

[The Belmont Report (1979)](https://www.hhs.gov/ohrp/regulations-and-policy/belmont-report/read-the-belmont-report/index.html)  |  [UNESCO, Universal Declaration on Bioethics and Human Rights](https://www.unesco.org/en/legal-affairs/universal-declaration-bioethics-and-human-rights)

